name o4-09-night-1
timeout 300

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 9 OF 10 — THE OTHER HALF OF THE CONCESSION, AND THE SPEC LISTED IT AS THE ONE
# MISSION THAT CANNOT BE FLOWN. doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md mission 9. It is now RUNNABLE and it
# is still not ANSWERABLE, and the difference between those two words is what this file measures.
#
# WHAT CHANGED SINCE THE SPEC. The spec blocked this mission on `C2` (no time of day) and, more deeply,
# on `C3` (no visual channel for darkness to degrade). BOTH are closed: `time <ISO8601 Z>` is mission
# data (doc/missions/syntax.md) and sensors/FBVisualSystem is built and is the sixth registry reader
# (doc/sensors.md §9). So the file below is o4-04-entry-10nm.fbm plus ONE mission-wide line — the clock
# — and fresh callsigns.
#
# WHAT DID NOT CHANGE. NOTHING CONSUMES THE VISUAL BLOCK. pilot/FBPilot never reads it, exactly as it
# never reads the Irst block (doc/duels.md D3). And there is no aircraft-lighting model, so at night the
# channel contributes nothing at all — which is the model and not a bug (doc/missions/sensors.md,
# "at night it contributes nothing"). The two consequences are the mission's whole content:
#   a. FBDaylightFactor is a smoothstep in sun elevation that reaches ZERO at -9 deg
#      (core/FBEphemeris.h). At 55.20 N on 1997-12-10 at 22:00Z the sun sits far below that, so the
#      eye's day factor is 0 and no visual contact can form.
#   b. Because no pilot reads the block, every flight column of this run must be IDENTICAL to o4-04's.
#      That is the acceptance test of this mission, and a divergence in any column other than the
#      environment and visual ones would be a defect.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION, therefore, is not "who wins at night" — nothing in the tree can answer
# that. It is: HOW BIG IS THE HOLE? The answer is a column count and a contact count, and it is
# published beside the campaign result rather than dressed up as a tactical finding.
#
# THE DATE IS INSIDE THE ANCHOR'S OWN PERIOD (JG 73 operated the MiG-29G from 1991 to 2003) and it is
# December because December is when 55 N has a real night; the campaign's own clock, declared in
# o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.fbc, is a June morning. Both are [SET].
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29, both runs as campaign steps so both carry a clock): of 184 telemetry columns the
# night run differs from the daylight run in SIX, and every one of them is visual — `vis_glare` on both
# jets, plus `vis_contacts` / `vis_best_mrad` / `vis_best_az` / `vis_best_el` / `vis_best_state` on the
# MiG (50 rows each, RECOGNISED by day, nothing at night). Every flight, sensor, weapon and engagement
# column is byte-identical; both runs fire at the same instants from the same ranges and kill the same
# jet at the same tick (t=29.3, missM 1.65047). exit 0 either way. THAT NUMBER IS THE MISSION: darkness
# reaches six columns and no decision.
#
# READING RULE: the verdict is a DIFF, not an exit code. Compare this run's telemetry column by column
# against o4-04's: expect `blk_vis`/`vis_*` and the environment columns to differ and NOTHING else.
# Read `vis CONTACT`/`RECOGNISED`/`IDENTIFIED` counts (o4-04 has them, this file must have none) and the
# MISSION_START sun elevation. exit 2 would be a defect.

time 1997-12-10T22:00:00Z

unit viper8
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 13.45420 5000 90.0 380       # 10.00 nm apart, head-on, co-altitude
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9                            # firing order: the infrared rounds first
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 5000 380               # hulkeast: the MiG's own range target
  objective kill unit fulcrum8
  objective survive

unit fulcrum8
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.20000 13.74580 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode acm                           # briefed INTO the fight: the close-combat auto-lock volume
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set kols_mode ir_cc                         # the KOLS in its close-combat field — the third of the
  set kols_laser on                           # quotation's three reasons, and the one o4-08 can blind
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 55.20000 12.60000 5000 380               # hulkwest: the F-16's own range target
  objective kill unit viper8
  objective survive

unit hulkwest
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 55.20000 12.60000 ground 90.0 0

unit hulkeast
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 55.20000 14.60000 ground 270.0 0
